      "role": "user",
      "content": "Actually, that's not quite what I meant. I'm more worried about the part where it says \"unaided memory.\" \n\nIf I'm working on their codebase and I learn a really specific way to optimize a data processing loop or a certain architectural pattern that works well for their scale, can I actually use that same logic for my next client? Or does the \"Confidential Information\" part prevent me from using those general coding patterns I've now \"memorized\"?",
